  "_provenance_note": "Post-Fase-2A measurement (rag-embedding-contract, Phases 1-6 applied), run twice — both runs byte-identical since FakeEmbedder is deterministic and this config has no other source of randomness. Saved under a distinguishing filename rather than the harness's default '2026-08-10-fake.json' because that name is already the frozen PRE-fix baseline recorded at this change's Phase 0 gate (same UTC calendar date — the harness dates by UTC, and both runs landed in the same session); overwriting it would destroy the 'before' reference this comparison depends on. Compare against docs/eval/results/2026-08-10-fake.json: aggregate recall@1 0.100->0.200, recall@5 0.600->0.500, recall@10 1.000->1.000 (unchanged), mrr 0.3087->0.3429, ndcg@10 0.4684->0.4913. recall@1 is NOT a clean +2: two exact-text-match cases (c01, c02) flipped 0.0->1.0, but one case (c07, the query about the L2-vs-cosine concern itself) regressed 1.0->0.0 — the net is +1 case out of 10 (two gains minus one loss), not two gains alone. recall@5 churned rather than moved: 9 of the 10 scored cases changed recall@5 between the two runs (4 gained: c01, c02, c04, c09; 5 lost: c05, c06, c07, c08, c13; only c03 held steady) — the net -1 case (0.600->0.500) is the difference of two much larger, opposite-signed movements, not one case's tail sliding, and n=10 cannot support any conclusion about recall@5 from a swing that size. Ranking is dominated by ties rather than query similarity on both sides of the fix: the mean positional agreement between each case's ranked_refs and the most common (modal) ordering across all 10 cases is ~0.69 post-fix and ~0.68 pre-fix — roughly 69% of each case's ranking is the same regardless of which query was asked, in both runs, because FakeEmbedder's near-orthogonal unit vectors make the tier/decay/importance/dispute product dominate over the now much smaller cosine spread. Distinct orderings across the 10 cases fell from 12 (pre-fix) to 10 (post-fix), so the MAX(0.0, ...) clamp on cosine_from_l2_unit added ties rather than resolving them. Net: --fake does not discriminate retrieval quality well enough for its recall@5/mrr/ndcg@10 deltas to be read as evidence the embedding contract fix improved or regressed ranking — only the recall@1 exact-match behavior and the qualitative bound (scores now finite and non-negative instead of frequently negative) are trustworthy signals from this harness; --real remains the only mode where a movement would be attributable to the fix rather than to tie noise."
